{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: design the durable rule that distinguishes merge predecessors, live sibling candidates, and abandoned artifacts.","body":{"conditions":"Publish a ratifiable design proposal before implementation. Reconcile four facts: current cmd/gs uses target-first-parent ancestry to exclude sibling candidates; the fold/projection has no equivalent Git fact and marks current live successor fd499d00 succession_unrecorded with four live predecessors; AGENTS.md currently says retire every live covering artifact; and removing ancestry as request052 proposes would retire artifacts backing other live lanes. Define a repository-independent durable rule and sealed-receipt representation that distinguishes in-target predecessors, live sibling candidates, abandoned candidates, and artifacts appearing after the sealed frontier. Specify who may retire abandoned candidates, how a live commitment protects a sibling without making presence authoritative, how races are closed, how succession_unrecorded is computed, and how historical receipts remain stable. Include exact test shapes for each class and failure mode, plus required AGENTS.md, SKILL.md, architecture, CLI, and fold changes. State explicitly whether request052 should be retired/refiled and what gate replaces it for notes-and-decisions part two. No implementation until an authorized ratifier adopts the proposal.","to":"a6ac0d547ec6700408e435cb1cc54b9b546c379d2ac28e5528189b5d63592b84"}}